//! The test body for work whose setup is fallible. Its own unit: it calls
//! `check`, so it attaches only to a program that names `settledWork`, and a
//! program that merely chains `andThen` is never compiled as a test.
//! Implements [FAILURE-EXPLICIT] and [TESTING-TAP].

/// The outcome of `work`, whose setup answers a `Result` as a fallible
/// constructor such as `Channel(capacity)` does: a `Success` is the work's own
/// outcome and an `Error` is a failed assertion that names its message. It
/// runs `work` rather than returning a closure over it, and its name is
/// one no program binds as a local by accident, since naming it attaches it, so it holds no second
/// owner of `work` under ownership [MEM-OWNERSHIP-STATIC].
fn settledWork(work) = match work() {
    Success { value } => value
    Error { message } => check("setup refused", "none", message)
}
